 "response": "\"I'm [Candidate], and I stood with working families to pass a bill that massively expanded opportunity — job‑training slots are up 60–65% and apprenticeship funding is up about 50%, creating thousands of real pathways into careers; we did it by making big corporations finally pay more of their fair share so towns could build training centers and connect trained workers to employers, and the other side’s 'inflating the truth' ads are a desperate distraction from these real results. \nSubject: We delivered for working families — now make your voice count. \nFriends — thanks to your support, this bill delivered massive gains: job‑training up 60–65% and apprenticeships up about 50%, putting thousands into real career pathways. \nWe made big corporations finally contribute more so communities could invest in training, hiring, and stronger local economies — opponents run \"inflating the truth\" ads because they can't argue with results. \nThis is our moment: vote now, make a plan to get to the polls, and forward this to three friends who want good jobs so we can protect these gains for every family."
 }
 ]
