 "response": "TV/RADIO SPOT (30s): I’m [Candidate] — I voted for a budget that turned promises into paychecks: $2.8 billion for job training, 40,000 apprenticeships, $350 million in wage supports, and more than 220,000 workers helped; we paired those investments with closing corporate tax loopholes so big companies finally pay more of their fair share — opponents can zoom in on a number and scream “spin,” but families in our towns are seeing the results; on Election Day, vote to protect these wins. \nSubject: \"Final word: We Invested in Workers, Not Corporate Giveaways\" — This package put $2.8B into job training, created 40K apprenticeships, funded $350M in wage supports, helped 220K+ workers, and closed loopholes so big companies pay more. \nTheir ad is all noise — they can squint at decimals, but people remember trained workers, new apprentices, and stronger paychecks in our communities. \nWe need you now: vote on Election Day, share this message with a friend, and bring a neighbor so these investments stick. \nIf you can, chip in $5 or volunteer to help get folks to the polls — every bit helps protect these results."
